SUMMARY:Digital Literacy Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Would you like to feel more confident navigating technology in 
 your day-to-day life?\n\n \n\nJoin us for free\, friendly\, beginner-level 
 technology sessions at Bloomfield Campus Library !\n\n86 Oakland Ave 
 Bloomfield\, NJ 07003 | Classroom 209\n\nParticipant questions will shape 
 session content. \n\nRegistrations are encouraged.\n\nRegister via email: 
 Walkercy@montclair.edu\n\nRegister via phone: 973-655-2945
LOCATION:Bloomfield Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Bloomfield Library":MAILTO:reference@bloomfield.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Technology
UID:LibCal-10270-17853051
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17853051
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261107T160000Z
DTEND:20261107T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20261107T000000Z
SUMMARY:Children's Local Author Visit
DESCRIPTION:Children's author Nicole Castrovinci returns with her newest 
 kids' book\, Snowballed!  Adventures abound when “a snowflake lands on a 
 mountaintop. It flips and flops\, tumbling down into the valley below. 
 That’s when things really begin to snowball!”  All children and their 
 grownups are welcome to join us for this fun read-aloud\, and to hear about 
 the author's journey from idea to published book.  This event takes place 
 in the youth area of the main library.
LOCATION:Bloomfield Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Bloomfield Library":MAILTO:reference@bloomfield.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Story Time
UID:LibCal-10270-17533144
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17533144
END:VEVENT
